AMLP LPC driver -- test session

This mudlib exists to exercise real driver functionality (movement,
commands, persistence, the eval command) end to end over a live
connection. It is not a themed game.

Commands you can actually run here:
  say <text>     speak to everyone in your room
  who            list connected players
  eval <code>    compile and run one LPC statement, e.g.
                 eval return 1 + 1;
  help           show this list again
  quit           save and disconnect
  shutdown       stop the whole driver process

Movement (each room's own description lists its real exits):
  north / south / east / west

Once you are holding the wand of creation (handed to you automatically
in the entrance hall):
  clone <path>   clone an existing .c file into this room or your
                 inventory
  purge <name>   destruct a named object in the room
  create <name>  generate and place a brand-new, minimal object
